UNIT explain_diff
LANG ts
PRIMARY-SHA256 b247f386a1f76aed3899519b572965ca540167a0d571a6666a6f99ccc7041cd5
SIG export function explain_diff(before: string, after: string, oracleChanged: boolean | null, langs: readonly string[]): Review
ABI TypeScript compiles to the js runtime and is driven exactly as js: four positional values, the artifact a named export.
  Declare in the artifact
  type Piece = { op: '=' | '-' | '+'; text: string };
  type Change = { section: string; id: string; label: string; kind: 'changed' | 'added' | 'removed'; checked: boolean;
  text?: string; diff?: Piece[]; whyDiff?: Piece[] | null };
  type Warning = { level: 'stop' | 'ok' | 'note'; kind: string; text: string };
  type Review = { unit: string; changes: Change[]; warnings: Warning[] }.
  Optional keys are omitted, never written as undefined: text on added and removed items; diff and whyDiff (null when the
  raw citation lists are equal) on changed items. text = string (UTF-16; R18's cut counts code points, Array.from(q));
  none = null. STRICT: the artifact type-checks under strict: true with no any, no non-null assertions (!), no @ts-ignore
  and no @ts-expect-error. ES module, imports nothing; never mutates langs.
MECHANISM (restated from js — language files are self-contained) WS (R15 R16) is exactly the ECMAScript \s class and
  String.prototype.trim's set; spaces and tabs are [ \t]. R2's line
  cut is split(/\r\n|\r|\n/); space/tab fields (R8) are split(/[ \t]+/) with the empty pieces filtered out. The LINE
  SEPARATOR and PARAGRAPH SEPARATOR characters are written as the escapes \u2028 and \u2029, never raw, in any source literal.
MECHANISM fixed tables (TABLE PIN-KINDS, OTHER-LABELS, KNOWN-OTHER, R17's language names) are a ReadonlyMap<string, string>,
  a ReadonlySet<string> or an Object.hasOwn test — never a plain indexed object read, which reaches inherited members. The
  after index (R12, R14) is a Map<string, Item> keyed by section and id; group by section plus id with exactly " #" + digits removed from the end. A Map.get result is Item |
  undefined; narrow it with an explicit undefined test. R12's numbering counts base ids across the whole version.
MECHANISM DIFF (R15) needs only the LCS table; build it as (n+1) x (m+1) number arrays filled from the end.
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex COMMENT-LEAD = /^#+[ \t]?/ CITED R9 — removed from a comment line that belongs to a directive
PINNED regex REF-TAIL = /[.,;:)\]]+$/ CITED R18 — removed from each citation token before it is compared to a REF
PINNED regex ATTR = /[ \t]+(CITED|EARNED|ANCHOR)(?=[ \t]|$)/g CITED R5 — a hit whose keyword starts inside a quoted span is skipped
PROVENANCE rederive@9b9e5d24ca9d cli/lsp/explain.mjs and cli/sir/sir-parse.mjs (the regexes above are the real code's).
  Language file cut 2026-11-02 with the primary and revised with it on the re-pin, before any blind re-emission.
